      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High-temperature oxidation of the Hf-rich coating will produce a dense, slowly growing HfO2 surface layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting HfO2 scale will be continuous and adherent.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Zr will diffuse from the substrate into the Hf-rich coating and create a graded Hf-Zr interfacial region.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf oxidizes preferentially to form stable HfO2.",
